    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d198-a3">

                <pb facs="0625" n="567" sameAs="frus:frus1866p3/pg567"/>

                <head>Mr. Hunter to Mr.
                        Burton</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 154.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <hi
                                rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1866-08-31"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >August</hi> 31, 1866.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have to acknowledge the receipt of your
                    despatch, No. 247, of the 26th of last June, giving the limitations proposed by
                    the President of Panama to the right of transit of the United States over the
                    isthmus of Darien, and giving it as your opinion that the proposed change has
                    been abandoned.</p>
                <p>The United States must be understood as not assenting to this proposed change in
                    the orders of the President of Panama of May 13th, 1865. But it is, perhaps,
                    best to avoid all unnecessary discussion of the matter.</p>
                <p>I am, sir, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>W. HUNTER, <hi rendition="#italic">Acting
                    Secretary</hi>.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Allan A. Burton</hi>, Esq., &amp;<hi
                            rendition="#italic">c</hi>., &amp; <hi rendition="#italic">c</hi>.,
                        &amp; <hi rendition="#italic">c</hi>.</p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
